course: dictionary
lesson: 12936
title: Evidential
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Evidence is the facts that show whether something is true. A detective collects evidence, and so does a scientist testing an idea. «Evidential» is the describing word: it means to do with evidence, or serving as evidence. «The muddy boot print was evidential, because it matched the thief's shoe.» The print is a fact that helps show who was there, so it is evidential.
explain: The "-ial" ending is a clue. Words like "official" and "essential" also end this way and describe something. Evidence is the noun, and evidential describes something connected with it. Ask yourself: does this thing help prove or support the idea? If yes, it may be evidential.
explain: In law, evidential value is how much a fact or object helps prove something in court. «The judge said the torn ticket had strong evidential value, because it showed the seat was booked at noon.» A thing can have high or low evidential value: a strong fact helps a lot, and a weak fact helps very little.
fact: Evidence means facts, objects or signs that show whether something is true.
fact: «Evidential» means to do with evidence, or serving as evidence.
fact: «Evidential value» means how much a fact or object helps prove something in court.
fact: Phrases like evidential weight and evidential basis are used in law, science and history to talk about how strong the evidence is.
fact: Evidence is the noun and evidential is the describing word. Pupils will meet «evidence» far more often, so learn that one first.
exercise: «The muddy boot print was evidential, because it matched the thief's shoe.» What does evidential mean here? | *To do with evidence, helping to show who was there | To do with mud and rain | Very old and valuable | Something a thief would wear
exercise: «The judge said the torn ticket had strong evidential value.» What does evidential value mean? | *How much a fact or object helps prove something in court | How long a ticket is kept | How many people saw the ticket | How much money a ticket costs
exercise: Which word is the describing word (adjective) made from evidence? | *evidential | evidence | proving | evidently
test: «The photo was evidential, showing the car was parked outside the bank.» Which word is closest in meaning to evidential? | Expensive | Hidden | Blurry | *Related to evidence
test: Scientists test an idea and collect facts. Which of these is evidential? | A favourite colour | A guess with no facts | A made-up story | *A measurement that shows whether the idea is true
exam: Ella says a lawyer wants the receipt to show the shop sold the bike. Why is the receipt evidential? | Because it is long and white | Because it is made of paper | Because the shop is near the bank | *Because it is a fact that helps prove what happened
